{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS9ihcmtgPKagPwibgUq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish failed because the similarity score was a Python float, and DynamoDB rejects floats. The fix is in place and the tests pass. The cause and fix are written up in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Cause:** Every story is stored with a `similar` list of `{slug, score}`. `similarity()` returned a float. The first publish is fine because the library is empty, so no score is written. The second publish has one story to compare against, so a float goes into the item. boto3 raises `TypeError: Float types are not supported`, and `handler()` turns that into a 500.\n\n**Fix:** `similarity()` in `src/app.py` now returns a `Decimal`.\n\n**Keeping it from coming back:** The existing test only published into an empty table, so it never hit the float path. I added two tests in `tests/test_publish.py`:\n- A test that publishes two overlapping stories through `handler()` and expects a 201 on the second.\n- A test that pins `similarity()` to return a `Decimal`.\n\nBoth new tests fail on the original code and pass with the fix. `python3 -m unittest discover tests` passes all three tests.\n\nNothing was deployed or published. The story from the log that returned 500 at 09:21:47 was never stored, so it needs to be published again once the fix ships."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1079,"cache_read_input_tokens":31434,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1079},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb02f831-5a72-43fe-a56d-7039c8910aab","uuid":"52b193ae-1693-4141-9fbd-5cbe659c73f5","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:59:06.800Z","requ